endobj
1201 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (____Climate risks exacerbate pressures on the healthcare system, leading to increased injuries and greater vulnerability of the sector during heatwaves and outbreaks of climate-sensitive and infectious diseases. Social differentiation is a critical factor to take into account in adaptation reponses. Women in rural areas often have limited access to resources, technologies, and decision-making processes, which constrains their ability to respond effectively to climate shocks. Social norms and gender roles may further restrict access to information, finance, and mobility, thereby reinforcing existing inequalities. Therefore, adaptation policies need to be gender-responsive and socially inclusive, considering differences across gender, age, and physiological characteristics.)
/E (____Climate risks exacerbate pressures on the healthcare system, leading to increased injuries and greater vulnerability of the sector during heatwaves and outbreaks of climate-sensitive and infectious diseases. Social differentiation is a critical factor to take into account in adaptation reponses. Women in rural areas often have limited access to resources, technologies, and decision-making processes, which constrains their ability to respond effectively to climate shocks. Social norms and gender roles may further restrict access to information, finance, and mobility, thereby reinforcing existing inequalities. Therefore, adaptation policies need to be gender-responsive and socially inclusive, considering differences across gender, age, and physiological characteristics.)
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
